1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,528
This film is also its own demonstration. Every timestamp comes from one storyboard and the measured duration of the real narration, never from a hand estimate.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:26,160
Before, every regenerated voice meant editing index dot HTML, captions, manifests, and project metadata separately. If one MP3 ran longer than its slide, the final video cut the narration short.

3
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:40,048
Now there is one pipeline. The storyboard produces the script, Edge TTS creates each MP3, ffprobe measures its real length, and sync updates the page, captions, and metadata together.

4
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:54,312
Render waits behind two gates. H F audit checks project structure, schema, and audio cut risk. HyperFrames check then verifies runtime behavior, layout, motion, and text contrast.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,440
Automation does not replace a person. Someone still has to hear the pacing and pronunciation, inspect readability, and approve that specific language before render.

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,840
From storyboard to video through one rerunnable pipeline. This is Snowy HyperFrames Workflow version two.
